        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Mn(NO3)2·4H2O (0.1 g, 0.39 mmol), Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (0.1 g, 0.22 mmol), and tetrahydrocalix[4]arene 5 (0.1 g, 0.23 mmol) were dissolved in DMF (10 cm3) and MeOH (10 cm3). The mixture was stirred for 5 min, then NEt3 (0.2 g, 1.97 mmol) was added dropwise. The resulting purple solution was stirred for an additional hour. X-ray quality purple/black crystals of 6 were obtained after slow evaporation of the mother liquor.",
