      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Dc susceptibility of the isotropic Mn4Gd4 cluster 6 shows a room-temperature χMT close to the uncoupled spin-only value; magnetization does not saturate even at 70 kG and reduced-magnetization isofield lines are nearly superimposable. A large magnetocaloric effect is observed, with −ΔSm = 19.0 J kg−1 K−1 at 4 K for ΔH = 70 kG, exceeding the entropy of an isolated S = 22 ground state because of populated low-lying excited spin states, making 6 a candidate molecular refrigerant.",
